  "slug": "archaea-duplication-d927",
  "summary": "New tools and resources infer coding alignments, protein complex orthogroups and family trees across many genomes, plus a C. elegans annotation explorer.",
  "synthesis": "Three items define genomic and proteomic content from cross-genome comparison rather than a single reference annotation. Genomes2Genes converts Progressive Cactus whole-genome alignments into validated coding sequence alignments for extant and ancestral species. The Genome Biology and Evolution study maps verified protein complex components to orthogroups across 31 eukaryotes, identifies 184 universal orthogroups, and releases the PCOC suite for detecting expansions. PANTHER 2027 extends its phylogenetic protein family trees to 131 genomes, with revised families and 20%-100% gain in GO annotation coverage. These differ in scope, data type and goal, so the shared element is strategy, not method. WormIE is a more peripheral item: a browser tool integrating C. elegans annotations for gene-list and RNA-seq interpretation, including curated neuronal and synaptic gene sets.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-17"
}
